# Headers for static hosts that read this file (Cloudflare Pages and Netlify both do; other hosts
# simply ignore it). It is not a build step and nothing reads it locally.
#
# Why Cache-Control: no-cache: the app has no build step, so no file name carries a content hash and a
# long cache would keep serving last week's JavaScript after a deploy — the stale-module problem the
# owner already hit once (fixed locally by dev-server.py, which sends no-store). "no-cache" means
# "store it, but check with the server before using it", so a deploy is picked up on the next load.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: same-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
